If you would like to contribute code to this project you can do so through GitHub by forking the repository and sending a pull request.

Before Comcast accepts your code into the project you must sign the Comcast Contributor License Agreement (CLA).

If you haven�t previously signed a Comcast CLA, we can e-mail you a PDF that you can sign and scan back to us. 

Please send us an e-mail or create a new GiHhub issue to request a PDF version of the CLA.

When editing a file with an existing Oscar copyright banner, preserve its original
start year and extend the range through the current calendar year. For example,
Copyright 2015 becomes Copyright 2015 - 2026 for changes made in 2026. A banner
starting in the current year can retain that single year. Do not add banners to
files without one, or alter third-party notices or bundled specification sources.

The code hygiene gate checks banners in staged, unstaged and untracked files.
Run only this check with tools/code-hygene-checker.sh --copyright-only.
To check explicit paths (for example in CI), append them after --copyright-only.
